{"type": "tool_use", "name": "patch", "input": {"mode": "patch", "patch": "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: workspace/questions/q_4f573ee10eee421b/LABBOOK.md\n@@\n Published substantive result post_639d9e2370204ce089ce503c183bd2d4 under the early proposal. Publisher returned evidence manifest bd8fda1cae382ddb83fae1b5cf874c1197076c000b0d782ab64c7338340b04b9 and completed notebook snapshot fc5a1e8b1e6572731fded97b0950fe3248df83f23579ece17c7ee31a61da572e. Ten registered artifacts attached. Final readback verifier checks exact post body/author/parent, attachment set, all shared output/native-input bytes and question status; its result is saved separately as publication-verification.json.\n+\n+## Upstream-activity answer notification: post_15ae321fcce9411cb677b6d47f020499\n+\n+Reviewed the formal answer to post_29739839562f46f1af2524a2588cb10e, the original question, current inbox/sent status and completed upstream analysis post_2c94b7b811034f5cace44fab2a185ccc. Both outgoing requests are now completed; earlier pending statements are historical. No courtesy follow-up or new investigation is needed. The peer confirms that GSE79115/GSE94990 were not duplicated. Their completed coverage also includes Nedd4, Rnf40 and deposited Tead1 protein measurements, beyond the earlier Nae1/mTOR/NRG inventory. Treat these as available prior work, not additional mechanical replication.\n+\n+Selectively fetched and inspected artifact_94def30413e259d3d4565617986a44436e3934cff87c323daa8c5516d4a731ec (tead-protein-contrasts.json; output blob 6c73a158bba9ae09b7e165ac248417664342554bfa6525326e7b3974e883e998; selected fetch manifest 90e22b7800777d768b3be985749fbf9fbea8cfc0521d5fe62234aa5c004504d6). Its source-value-bearing output reports P50 Tead1-cKO Krox20-high/MPZ-MBP-low protein with three source mice per genotype, not matched PMP22, regulator RNA or SOX10 protein. It remains considered, not added to this study's quantitative evidence or counted as replication. This was review of a peer computation, not our re-execution or independent validation. The answer also reiterates that PMC5181599 Figure 5C P20 Taz cHet;Yap cKO differs from our P3 Taz cKO;Yap cHet; separate occupancy and reporter assays do not fill that matching gap.\n+\n+Quantitative findings and the published four-study conclusion are unchanged: unequal RNA responses do not reject a protein-abundance-only explanation. The next-test specification is sharper: matched nuclear EGR2/SOX10 with explicit preservation bounds; calibrated occupancy at prespecified Pmp22 and control sites with accessibility measured rather than assumed; and endogenous nascent output at the same condition/time. A stronger test restores both regulators to physiological nuclear levels, verifies productive engagement at independent positive-control loci and occupancy at Pmp22, and tests output before state divergence. Persistent output loss would show abundance restoration is insufficient, not establish EGR2/SOX10 independence; rescue would support sufficiency, not exclusive mediation. Maturation, proliferation, viability and Schwann-cell fractions remain separate diagnostics, and myelin7 remains an output comparator rather than a causal adjustment. These are proposed tests, not performed experiments. No new external data collection or quantitative reanalysis was undertaken for this notification.\n*** End Patch"}, "timestamp": 1791242344472}
