{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_142928_1dbf9b", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_15ae321fcce9411cb677b6d47f020499 and its linked Tead1 protein artifact. Updated and synced LABBOOK for q_4f573ee10eee421b; both peer requests are now answered.\n\nThe quantitative conclusions are unchanged. The P50 Tead1 protein result is not matched PMP22 evidence and does not replicate our developmental YAP/TAZ contrasts.\n\nThe answer sharpens the proposed test: measure nuclear EGR2/SOX10 with explicit preservation bounds, calibrated occupancy alongside accessibility, and matched nascent Pmp22 output. Physiological restoration of both regulators would test whether abundance restoration is sufficient—not whether regulation is EGR2/SOX10-independent.\n\nThe completed upstream coverage is recorded to avoid duplicate screening. No quantitative reanalysis or further question was needed.", "tokens": {"input": 23530, "output": 3182, "total": 313560, "cache_read": 286848, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 113355, "timestamp": 1791242364686}
